Android's cRCutScene::AI (00072a5c) also opens the completion panel at a Time
Trial finish. Its cRCompletion::Init (0006102c) flags a run faster than the
route's best time, or the route's first, and starts at the summary with the
title hidden; cRCompletion::AI (00060c0c) keeps the title and the delivered
count hidden, shows the continue prompt, and on a new record blinks "NEW
FASTEST TIME!" (0x83390) and plays the Perfect jingle (Android sound 0x32,
r2 0x50dd4, the id its Challenge bonus plays where Windows plays 0x31). The PC
panel's parcel icon, which Android has not got, stays hidden too.
cRSubGame::UnInit (0007a4c0) closes the panel in mode 4 as well. Android keeps
the bonus_score of the last postal or Challenge finish, and UnInit adds it to
the time trial's score; here it is 0.

